        "title": "About Space Exploration",
        "subject": "Space Exploration",
        "summary": "The event centers on SpaceX’s Starship Flight 15 test, which demonstrated recovery of the Starship upper stage at Starbase, Texas after an orbital mission. The result is significant because SpaceX is developing Starship as a two-stage system intended for rapid reuse, while NASA’s Voyager 1 milestone illustrates a separate, long-running strand of space exploration: robotic science beyond the heliosphere.",
        "facts": [
          {
            "label": "Mission timing and location",
            "value": "Flight 15 launched from SpaceX’s Starbase site near Boca Chica in Cameron County, Texas, on November 13, 2026; the Starship upper stage returned to the site and was caught by the launch tower on November 14. The selected timeline’s November 15 date reflects subsequent reporting rather than the capture’s calendar date.",
            "source_ids": [
              "o1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Vehicle format",
            "value": "Starship is a two-stage launch system comprising the Starship upper stage and the Super Heavy booster. SpaceX’s stated design approach is for both stages to return to Earth and be caught by mechanical arms on the launch tower for inspection, refurbishment, and reuse.",
            "source_ids": [
              "o2"
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Test outcome",
            "value": "The upper stage completed an orbital flight and was recovered at the launch tower, while the Super Heavy booster diverted to a water landing rather than completing its planned tower catch.",
            "source_ids": [
              "o1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Regulatory setting",
            "value": "Commercial Starship/Super Heavy launches from Boca Chica are regulated by the Federal Aviation Administration’s Office of Commercial Space Transportation. FAA licensing reviews address public safety, national-security and foreign-policy concerns, insurance, and environmental effects.",
